<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original Candy AI comparisons, primary sources, updates, adult boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Every page must answer a real reader question. Keywords belong in clear titles, headings, direct answers, and natural explanations—not repetition or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link to Candy AI's official site and policies where possible. We separate subscription access from token spending, avoid presenting marketing as independent test results, and require live verification for changing features and prices.</p><h2>Adult boundaries</h2><p>Coverage concerns adults and emphasizes consenting fictional scenarios, authorized media, privacy, cost visibility, and emotional boundaries. We never request private chats, credentials, or intimate personal images.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Requests should identify the URL, disputed statement, and a direct source supporting the correction.</p></InfoPage>
